    "created_at": "2025-11-18T14:54:06Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-11-18T14:54:06Z",
    "body": "Ah, there is a scenario. First you create an element with a registry, but don't connect it. Then you define it. This doesn't upgrade it because it's not connected. Then you run initialize. While initialize won't change the registry, it will upgrade it. I don't think https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/56034 currently tests this, but it should be easy to add as a follow-up.",
